{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966782,"nonce":"0h3E7GG5/lFN6WtfnyXKMwsY7/Y=","title":"canvas_demo's \\\"Canvas Text\\\" sample renders the background plate but not the headings —","message":"canvas_demo's `text_in_canvas()` (Demo 7) renders the dark background plate (the canvas's `ctx.fill_rect(0,0,bounds.w,bounds.h,...)`) but none of the three `ctx.draw_text` calls produce visible text. The card title above (\"Canvas Text\") renders normally — only the canvas-emitted text is missing.\n\nSymptoms confirmed on `feat/phase4-real-cache-scissor` after the Phase 4 work landed. Not confirmed whether pre-existing on PR #43 (`5fe2c983`); the user opted not to test that to save time.\n\n\n1. **Glyph-atlas rebind before `composite_frame`** (commit `8d834482`). Hypothesis: `collect_canvas_overlay` invokes canvas closures whose `draw_text` calls grow the atlas after the slow path's `set_glyph_atlas`, so the SDF bind group references a stale atlas view. Added `rebind_glyph_atlas_for_overlay` helper called before each `composite_frame` site. Did not fix the symptom.\n\n\n- `ctx.draw_text` in a canvas closure (paint.rs:2743+) shapes text via `text_ctx.prepare_text_with_style`, then for each glyph: `GpuPrimitive::from_glyph(glyph)` builds a PRIM_TEXT primitive with UVs in `gradient_params`, color in `color`, type_info[0] = `PrimitiveType::Text` (7). Pushed into `active_batch.primitives` (not `batch.glyphs`).\n- Canvas closures in `collect_canvas_overlay` emit into a SCRATCH `GpuPaintContext`. `take_batch` drains its primitives into `overlay.primitives`.\n- `composite_frame` filters overlay primitives via `is_primitive_visible` (PRIM_TEXT type=7 bypasses viewport AABB cull). Sorts via `upload_sorted_primitives`. Categorizes PRIM_TEXT as `SdfPipelineCategory::Text`, which `draw_split_sdf` dispatches through `pipelines.sdf_core` (the regular variant, not the `_overlay` MSAA-sample-count-1 variant — passed `overlay: false`).\n- The SDF shader's PRIM_TEXT branch samples from glyph_atlas using `gradient_params` UVs.\n\n\n1. **`overlay: false` parameter to `draw_split_sdf` inside `composite_frame`** ([renderer.rs:4951+](crates/blinc_gpu/src/renderer.rs#L4951)). `composite_frame`'s overlay pass uses sample_count=1 (the surface) but `overlay: false` selects the MSAA pipeline variant. wgpu validation should catch this, but in practice the regular variant might be sample_count-agnostic and the issue lives elsewhere.\n\n2. **Atlas reallocation invalidates UV coordinates**, not just the view pointer. If `text_ctx` repacks glyphs into a larger atlas, the OLD glyph UVs (in primitives already emitted to overlay) reference positions that no longer match the new atlas layout. `set_glyph_atlas` fixes the view binding but not the UV correspondence. Plausible but would need confirmation by checking text_ctx's atlas growth strategy.\n\n3. **PRIM_TEXT primitives sample blank in the overlay pass for a reason specific to LoadOp::Load** (composite_frame uses LoadOp::Load to preserve the just-blitted static cache). The shader's PRIM_TEXT branch outputs `vec4(glyph_color.rgb, glyph_color.a * coverage)` — under LoadOp::Load with the surface's blend mode, if `coverage` is 0 the pixel is unchanged. If the atlas sample returns 0 because of the UV / atlas mismatch (Candidate 2) or a binding misalignment, the visible result is \"no text\".\n\n\nFor users hitting this in their own code: use `Text` widget for canvas-adjacent text instead of `ctx.draw_text` inside the canvas closure. Place a `text(\"...\")` element above or beside the canvas instead of inside it.\n\n\n1. Diff Phase 4 work against `5fe2c983` (PR #43 tip) — specifically check if PRIM_TEXT dispatched through composite_frame ever worked, or if this has been broken since the layer-compositor MVP (commit `c279556e`). git bisect between c279556e and HEAD on canvas_demo's Demo 7.\n2. Confirm or rule out the `overlay: false` parameter. Try `overlay: true` in `composite_frame`'s `draw_split_sdf` call.\n3. Confirm or rule out the UV-after-reallocation theory: log the atlas's view ptr + glyph UVs at canvas-emit time and at composite_frame time; check if UVs stayed valid.\n4. As a last resort, dispatch canvas-emitted PRIM_TEXT through `render_text` (the glyph pipeline) instead of the SDF pipeline — but that requires storing them as `GpuGlyph` not `GpuPrimitive`, which would need a separate canvas-glyph collection path.","files":null}]}